{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Daily report\n",
        "\n",
        "Run one date from download through the published bulletin. This path does not retrain models. It downloads the CAMS forecast, the OpenIFS control forecast, and the CAMS Policy city forecasts, then computes AQI and neural confidence and writes both the JSON bulletin and the PDF.\n",
        "\n",
        "Install the report environment before opening this notebook. The steps are in [docs/installation.md](../docs/installation.md): a CPU PyTorch wheel, `pip install -e \".[report]\"`, CDS API credentials, and `configs/local.yaml`. This notebook assumes that environment is already active.\n",
        "\n",
        "Set `REPORT_DATE` in the next cell. Dates use `YYYYMMDD` or `YYYY-MM-DD`. Existing files are reused, so running the notebook again for the same date does not download them again. Neural confidence uses the pretrained checkpoints and can run on CPU (`DEVICE = \"cpu\"`) or on a GPU (`DEVICE = \"cuda:0\"`).\n",
        "\n",
        "The same run from a shell is `airwise-daily --date 20260929 --device cpu`. The cells below keep the four steps separate so each product can be inspected. The map cells need `cartopy` in addition to the report install. They are only for display."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import sys\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import xarray as xr\n",
        "from IPython.display import FileLink, HTML, display\n",
        "from matplotlib.animation import FuncAnimation\n",
        "from matplotlib.colors import LogNorm\n",
        "\n",
        "cwd = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
        "repo_root = None\n",
        "for candidate in (cwd, *cwd.parents):\n",
        "    if (candidate / \"pyproject.toml\").is_file() and (candidate / \"src\" / \"airwise\").is_dir():\n",
        "        repo_root = candidate\n",
        "        break\n",
        "if repo_root is None:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Run this notebook from the AIr-wise repository.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "src = str(repo_root / \"src\")\n",
        "if src not in sys.path:\n",
        "    sys.path.insert(0, src)\n",
        "\n",
        "REPORT_DATE = \"20260929\"\n",
        "DEVICE = \"cpu\"\n",
        "\n",
        "json_path = repo_root / \"reports\" / f\"germany_{REPORT_DATE}.json\"\n",
        "pdf_path = json_path.with_suffix(\".pdf\")\n",
        "region_config = repo_root / \"configs\" / \"regions\" / \"germany.yaml\"\n",
        "cams_forecast_path = repo_root / \"data\" / \"cams_forecast\" / f\"{REPORT_DATE}.nc\"\n",
        "cams_aqi_path = repo_root / \"data\" / \"aqi\" / f\"{REPORT_DATE}.nc\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Repository: {repo_root}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Report date: {REPORT_DATE}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Device: {DEVICE}\")\n",
        "print(f\"JSON: {json_path}\")\n",
        "print(f\"PDF: {pdf_path}\")\n",
        "print(f\"CAMS forecast: {cams_forecast_path}\")\n",
        "print(f\"CAMS AQI: {cams_aqi_path}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Download inputs\n",
        "\n",
        "Download the CAMS Europe forecast, the OpenIFS 00z control forecast, and the Germany city source-receptor forecasts. Paths come from `configs/default.yaml`, with machine-specific overrides in `configs/local.yaml`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m airwise.cli.acquire --date {REPORT_DATE}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1.1 CAMS Europe forecast\n",
        "\n",
        "PM10 is shown on a log scale for each lead hour. The animation is rebuilt each time this cell runs and is not stored in the notebook."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import cartopy.crs as ccrs\n",
        "\n",
        "AQI_COLORS = [\"#50f0e6\", \"#50ccaa\", \"#f0e641\", \"#ff5050\", \"#960032\", \"#7d2181\"]\n",
        "AQI_LABELS = [\"Good\", \"Fair\", \"Moderate\", \"Poor\", \"Very Poor\", \"Extremely Poor\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def show_europe_animation(\n",
        "    field,\n",
        "    *,\n",
        "    frame_title,\n",
        "    cmap,\n",
        "    norm=None,\n",
        "    vmin=None,\n",
        "    vmax=None,\n",
        "    cbar_label=None,\n",
        "    ticks=None,\n",
        "    ticklabels=None,\n",
        "):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Animate one Europe field over its time dimension.\"\"\"\n",
        "    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16, 10))\n",
        "    ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1, projection=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n",
        "    mesh = ax.pcolormesh(\n",
        "        field.longitude,\n",
        "        field.latitude,\n",
        "        field.isel(time=0),\n",
        "        cmap=cmap,\n",
        "        norm=norm,\n",
        "        vmin=vmin,\n",
        "        vmax=vmax,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ax.coastlines(color=\"black\")\n",
        "    grid = ax.gridlines(draw_labels=True, linewidth=1, color=\"gray\", alpha=0.5, linestyle=\"--\")\n",
        "    grid.xlabel_style = {\"size\": 12}\n",
        "    grid.ylabel_style = {\"size\": 12}\n",
        "    colorbar = fig.colorbar(mesh, fraction=0.028, pad=0.05)\n",
        "    if cbar_label:\n",
        "        colorbar.set_label(cbar_label, fontsize=14)\n",
        "    colorbar.ax.tick_params(labelsize=12)\n",
        "    if ticks is not None:\n",
        "        colorbar.set_ticks(ticks)\n",
        "        colorbar.set_ticklabels(ticklabels)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def update(frame):\n",
        "        mesh.set_array(field.isel(time=frame).values.ravel())\n",
        "        ax.set_title(frame_title(frame), fontsize=16, pad=20)\n",
        "        return [mesh]\n",
        "\n",
        "    animation = FuncAnimation(\n",
        "        fig,\n",
        "        update,\n",
        "        frames=field.sizes[\"time\"],\n",
        "        blit=False,\n",
        "        interval=300,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    plt.close(fig)\n",
        "    display(HTML(animation.to_jshtml()))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "with xr.open_dataset(cams_forecast_path) as cams_forecast:\n",
        "    cams_pm10 = cams_forecast[\"pm10_conc\"].sel(level=0).load()\n",
        "\n",
        "positive = cams_pm10.values[cams_pm10.values > 0]\n",
        "pm10_min = float(np.nanmin(positive)) if positive.size else 1e-2\n",
        "pm10_max = float(np.nanmax(cams_pm10.values))\n",
        "show_europe_animation(\n",
        "    cams_pm10,\n",
        "    frame_title=lambda frame: f\"CAMS Europe forecast PM$_{{10}}$ (log) — lead hour {frame}\",\n",
        "    cmap=plt.get_cmap(\"Spectral_r\"),\n",
        "    norm=LogNorm(vmin=pm10_min, vmax=pm10_max),\n",
        "    cbar_label=r\"PM$_{10}$ [$\mu$g/m$^3$]\",\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Compute AQI\n",
        "\n",
        "Classify the downloaded CAMS concentrations with the European AQI thresholds. This step only reads the local forecast file."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m airwise.cli.aqi --date {REPORT_DATE}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2.1 European AQI\n",
        "\n",
        "PM10 AQI levels use the six European AQI colours, from Good to Extremely Poor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from matplotlib.colors import ListedColormap\n",
        "\n",
        "with xr.open_dataset(cams_aqi_path) as aqi_dataset:\n",
        "    aqi_pm10 = aqi_dataset[\"pm10_conc\"].load()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def aqi_frame_title(frame):\n",
        "    timestamp = pd.to_datetime(str(aqi_pm10.time.values[frame])).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n",
        "    return f\"European AQI forecast — {timestamp}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "show_europe_animation(\n",
        "    aqi_pm10,\n",
        "    frame_title=aqi_frame_title,\n",
        "    cmap=ListedColormap(AQI_COLORS),\n",
        "    vmin=0.5,\n",
        "    vmax=6.5,\n",
        "    ticks=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6],\n",
        "    ticklabels=AQI_LABELS,\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Compute neural confidence\n",
        "\n",
        "Run the pretrained model on the CAMS forecast and the OpenIFS control forecast. The published bulletin always includes these confidence scores."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m airwise.cli.confidence --date {REPORT_DATE} --device {DEVICE}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Write the bulletin\n",
        "\n",
        "`configs/regions/germany.yaml` selects the 16 German regions, their order, display names, and representative cities. Polygon geometry comes from `data/shapefile/NUTS_RG_10M_2024_3035.gpkg`. The PDF is written next to the JSON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m airwise.cli.report --date {REPORT_DATE} --region-config {region_config} --output {json_path} --device {DEVICE}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Open the PDF\n",
        "\n",
        "The link below opens `reports/germany_<date>.pdf`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(pdf_path)\n",
        "FileLink(str(pdf_path))"
      ]
    }
